    "### 2.5.2 N-Queens Problem\n",
    "\n",
    "From slides: Place N queens on N×N board so no two attack each other.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Variables**: $Q_i$ = column position of queen in row $i$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Domain**: $\\{1, 2, ..., N\\}$ for each $Q_i$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Constraints**:\n",
    "- Column: $\\forall i,j: Q_i \\neq Q_j$ (no two queens in same column)\n",
    "- Diagonal: $|Q_i - Q_j| \\neq |i - j|$ (no two queens on same diagonal)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def solve_n_queens(n=8):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Solve N-Queens using backtracking\n",
    "    Returns list of solutions (column positions)\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    def is_safe(board, row, col):\n",
    "        # Check column constraint\n",
    "        for i in range(row):\n",
    "            if board[i] == col:\n",
    "                return False\n",
    "            # Check diagonal constraints: |Q_i - Q_j| != |i - j|\n",
    "            if abs(board[i] - col) == abs(i - row):\n",
    "                return False\n",
    "        return True\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def backtrack(board, row):\n",
    "        if row == n:\n",
    "            solutions.append(board[:])\n",
    "            return\n",
    "        \n",
    "        for col in range(n):\n",
    "            if is_safe(board, row, col):\n",
    "                board[row] = col\n",
    "                backtrack(board, row + 1)\n",
    "                board[row] = -1  # Backtrack\n",
    "    \n",
    "    solutions = []\n",
    "    backtrack([-1] * n, 0)\n",
    "    return solutions\n",
    "\n",
    "def display_board(board):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Display N-Queens board\"\"\"\n",
    "    n = len(board)\n",
    "    for row in range(n):\n",
    "        line = ''\n",
    "        for col in range(n):\n",
    "            line += 'Q ' if board[row] == col else '. '\n",
    "        print(line)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Solve 8-Queens\n",
    "print(\"Solving 8-Queens problem...\")\n",
    "solutions = solve_n_queens(8)\n",
    "print(f\"Found {len(solutions)} solutions!\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"First solution:\")\n",
    "display_board(solutions[0])\n",
    "print(f\"\\nColumn positions: {solutions[0]}\")"
   ]
  },
