   "source": [
    "### 2.5.3 Graph Coloring Problem\n",
    "\n",
    "From slides: Color graph vertices so adjacent vertices have different colors.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Variables**: $n \\times k$ binary variables $X_{i,c}$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $X_{i,c} = 1$ if vertex $i$ has color $c$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Constraints**:\n",
    "1. Each node colored exactly once: $\\sum_{c=1}^k X_{i,c} = 1$\n",
    "2. Adjacent nodes different colors: $X_{i,c} + X_{j,c} \\leq 1$ for $(i,j) \\in E$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def graph_coloring(graph, num_colors):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Solve graph coloring using backtracking\n",
    "    graph: dict of adjacency lists\n",
    "    num_colors: maximum number of colors (k)\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    n = len(graph)\n",
    "    colors = [-1] * n  # -1 means uncolored\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def is_safe(vertex, color):\n",
    "        # Check if any adjacent vertex has same color\n",
    "        for neighbor in graph[vertex]:\n",
    "            if colors[neighbor] == color:\n",
    "                return False\n",
    "        return True\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def solve(vertex):\n",
    "        if vertex == n:\n",
    "            return True\n",
    "        \n",
    "        for color in range(num_colors):\n",
    "            if is_safe(vertex, color):\n",
    "                colors[vertex] = color\n",
    "                \n",
    "                if solve(vertex + 1):\n",
    "                    return True\n",
    "                \n",
    "                colors[vertex] = -1  # Backtrack\n",
    "        \n",
    "        return False\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if solve(0):\n",
    "        return colors\n",
    "    return None\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example: Color a simple graph\n",
    "graph = {\n",
    "    0: [1, 2],\n",
    "    1: [0, 2, 3],\n",
    "    2: [0, 1, 3],\n",
    "    3: [1, 2]\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "colors = graph_coloring(graph, 3)\n",
    "if colors:\n",
    "    print(\"Graph coloring solution:\")\n",
    "    for vertex, color in enumerate(colors):\n",
    "        print(f\"  Vertex {vertex}: Color {color}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"No solution with given number of colors\")"
   ]
  },
