    "## 2.7 Summary and Comparison\n",
    "\n",
    "### Algorithm Comparison\n",
    "\n",
    "| Algorithm | Complete | Optimal | Time | Space |\n",
    "|-----------|----------|---------|------|-------|\n",
    "| BFS | Yes | Yes* | $O(b^d)$ | $O(b^d)$ |\n",
    "| DFS | No | No | $O(b^m)$ | $O(bm)$ |\n",
    "| UCS | Yes | Yes | $O(b^{C^*/\\epsilon})$ | $O(b^{C^*/\\epsilon})$ |\n",
    "| Greedy | No | No | $O(b^m)$ | $O(b^m)$ |\n",
    "| A* | Yes** | Yes** | $O(b^d)$ | $O(b^d)$ |\n",
    "\n",
    "\* For uniform costs\n",
    "\** If heuristic is admissible/consistent\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Takeaways\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Uninformed search** explores blindly but guarantees completeness\n",
    "2. **Informed search** uses domain knowledge (heuristics) for efficiency\n",
    "3. **A* is optimal** with admissible heuristics - best of both worlds!\n",
    "4. **CSPs** model problems with variables, domains, and constraints\n",
    "5. **Local search** trades completeness for memory efficiency\n",
    "6. **Simulated annealing** escapes local optima via randomization"
   ]
  },
